-## Trust Boundaries
-
-| Boundary | Description |
-|----------|-------------|
-| Claude Code runtime → UserPromptSubmit hook | Hook receives user prompt text via stdin. Hook output is prepended to agent context. Worst case: adversary crafts a prompt that makes the hook inject malicious "context" into agent memory. |
-
-## STRIDE Threat Register
-
-| Threat ID | Category | Component | Disposition | Mitigation Plan |
-|-----------|----------|-----------|-------------|-----------------|
-| T-30.6-01-01 | E (Elevation of Privilege via prompt injection) | The hook injects snippet content into agent context — if snippet files are tampered with, the agent would receive adversarial instructions | mitigate | Snippet files under `.claude/context-snippets/` are committed to repo; any modification goes through PR review. Hook READS snippets lazy (no eval/exec). Content is static markdown, not code. Additional defense: existing `gsd-prompt-guard.js` scans `.planning/` writes for injection patterns — extending to `.claude/context-snippets/` is a v2.9+ enhancement. |
-| T-30.6-01-02 | D (DoS) | Hook runs on EVERY user prompt; could delay input if slow | mitigate | 3s timeout in the hook (per `30.5-RESEARCH.md §Code Examples Example 1`). settings.json sets 5s timeout on command. Regex patterns are literal (no catastrophic backtracking). Snippet reads are small (≤1200 chars). Worst case ~10ms overhead per prompt. |
-| T-30.6-01-03 | T (Tampering) | Adversary could write to `.planning/agent-drift/hook_failures.jsonl` | accept | Log is gitignored (Plan 30.5-00 Task 3). Append-only from hook. No blocker to normal operation; debugging-only trail. |
-| T-30.6-01-04 | I (Info Disclosure) | Hook stdout injection logs include first 3 patterns matched | accept | No PII in patterns (regex categories only). Context_hits.jsonl content is hit classifications, not prompt content. |
-
-**Summary:** Hook operates on dev-host only. Snippets are audited markdown in git. Hook never blocks, never executes user input as code. Main mitigation: keep snippet files in repo with PR review gating changes.
-</threat_model>
