-## Issues Encountered
-
-- **Pyenv global is `system`, so bare `python3.11` shim resolves via `pyenv: python3.11: command not found`.** The `.mcp.json` pins `"command": "python3.11"` — when Claude Code spawns the MCP server, PATH resolution will miss unless the user has `pyenv global 3.11.9` or an equivalent shim. Documented in the README's Troubleshooting section with 2 fallbacks: (a) `pyenv global 3.11.9`, (b) edit `.mcp.json` to point at the absolute `.venv/bin/python3.11` binary. Acceptance assumption A4 from RESEARCH.md acknowledged this risk.
-- **Pre-existing Finder-duplicate files** in `tools/checks/`, `.claude/hooks/`, etc. — already logged in 30.7-00-SUMMARY §Issues Encountered. They do not affect Plan 03 (server.py does not scan directories; it imports specific modules) but their presence inflates `git status` output noise.
