-## State of the Art
-
-| Old Approach | Current Approach | When Changed | Impact |
-|--------------|------------------|--------------|--------|
-| Hand-rolled JSON-RPC stdio server | `FastMCP` decorator API | `mcp` SDK 1.0 (2025) → FastMCP folded into official SDK | 10x less code, built-in schema gen |
-| MCP SSE transport | MCP Streamable HTTP | 2026-01 ish | SSE deprecated per `code.claude.com/docs/en/mcp` — does not affect us (we use stdio, not SSE). `[CITED]` |
-| `claude mcp add` CLI-only registration | `.mcp.json` project-scope committed to repo | Claude Code 2.x | Team-shareable, version-controlled. This is our path. `[CITED]` |
-| Ad-hoc tool description strings | Pydantic model + docstring → auto JSON Schema | FastMCP 1.x | Tool discovery is declarative. |
-| Python 3.9 compat for all tools | Python 3.10+ required for `mcp` SDK | `mcp` 1.0 | Forces explicit `python3.11` in `.mcp.json`. Our backend and CI are already on 3.11; only the host default `python3` is 3.9. |
-
-**Deprecated/outdated (do NOT use):**
-- `fastmcp` PyPI package (separate lineage). The official `mcp.server.fastmcp.FastMCP` has feature parity and no extra dep. `[VERIFIED: PyPI shows both; official path preferred]`
-- Manual stdin/stdout JSON framing — SDK handles Content-Length headers and LSP-style framing. Do not implement.
-- Writing to stdout for any purpose other than JSON-RPC responses. Use stderr. `[CITED: code.claude.com]`
