-## 8. Scaling Considerations
-
-| Scale | Adjustments |
-|-------|-------------|
-| 0-1k users (current) | Monolith FastAPI + per-user SQLite cache for `marge_fiscale`. SLM on-device, no scaling concern. |
-| 1k-100k users | Cache `MargeFiscaleBreakdown` server-side keyed by `profile_hash` (15min TTL). LLM tier-2 (BYOK) scales with user opt-in. SLM is free. |
-| 100k+ users | Move `compute_marge_fiscale` to async worker (Celery) for batch precompute on profile change. WebSocket for `Stream<ChatMessage>` if HTTP/2 streaming proves insufficient. |
-
-### First Bottleneck
-
-**`generateChat` HTTP timeout (55s)** under cold-start LLM load. Mitigation: streaming partial text via SLM tier-1 (already wired), so user sees output in <2s even when backend slow. Phase 42 streaming refactor improves perceived latency by yielding `typing` ChatMessage immediately.
-
-### Second Bottleneck
-
-**ConfidenceScorer Bayesian recompute** on every wizard answer (86 call-sites). Currently <50ms per call. If user spam-types in onboarding, debounce updates to 200ms.
