-### Pitfall 9: Touching CoachOrchestrator regresses the working text-only flow
-
-**What goes wrong:**
-Existing `CoachOrchestrator.respondTo()` has 3 paths (Anonymous, BYOK, ServerKey), 800 LOC, ~200 tests. Adding scene/canvas streaming touches the same orchestrator. Risks:
-- **Accidental bare-catch** — refactor introduces new `try { ... } catch(e) {}` that swallows errors that the old path would have surfaced. We just shipped FIX-05 (Wave 2+) reducing 388 → ~50 bare catches; can't backslide.
-- **Sentry breadcrumb gap** — old path emits `coach.start / coach.tool_call / coach.end` breadcrumbs. New Stream path forgets to emit `coach.tool_call`, so when a tool fails, debug context vanishes.
-- **Save_fact regression** — old flow has a known unsync bug (audit P0-4, fix in flight). If we refactor BEFORE save_fact unsync is wired, we entrench the bug. If we refactor AFTER but lose the fix, we re-create it. Sequential discipline matters.
-- **Anonymous path drops compliance disclaimer** — Anonymous path has its own disclaimer injection (per-message + footer). New Stream path reuses ServerKey path's disclaimer logic, which expects authenticated state, fails on Anonymous.
-- **Tool-call ordering** — old path: text → tool_call → text. New stream may emit `text` before `tool_call` finishes resolving → user sees "voici ta marge" then 2s later the tool errors → "désolé impossible de calculer" → contradiction.
-- **Test coverage decline** — orchestrator test suite written for Future contract. Stream contract tests are NEW. Devs delete obsolete tests instead of porting → test count goes from 200 to 80. CI green, app broken.
-
-**Why it happens:**
-Refactoring a service-of-services is hard. Devs underestimate the surface area. Memory.feedback_no_shortcuts_ever.md exists for exactly this reason. Without explicit "preserve invariants" doctrine, devs delete to "simplify".
-
-**How to avoid:**
-1. **Capture invariants up-front** — before Phase 42 line 1 of code, write `test/services/coach/orchestrator_invariants_test.dart` that locks the current behavior (3 paths, disclaimer, breadcrumbs, tool-call sequencing, error envelopes). Test count must be ≥ pre-refactor count + new Stream tests.
-2. **Preserve old API behind feature flag**: handoff says `FeatureFlags.chatVivant` already covers this — verify flag is OFF by default until device gate passes, on every path (Anonymous + BYOK + ServerKey).
-3. **Adapter pattern, not rewrite** — `Future<CoachResponse>` keeps working; new `Stream<ChatMessage>` is built BY adapting (see Pitfall 1). Minimum invasive surface.
-4. **Save_fact unsync (FIX-03 carry-forward) MUST be wired BEFORE Phase 42 line 1**. Sequential discipline — if not, we entrench the bug under a Stream layer where it's harder to debug.
-5. **Sentry breadcrumb parity test** — record breadcrumbs from old path on a known input, run new path on same input, assert breadcrumb sets match (ordering can differ, names+counts must match).
-6. **Disclaimer injection shared module** — extract into `compliance_disclaimer.dart` callable from both Future and Stream paths. Single source of disclaimers. Avoids "ServerKey path got the disclaimer, Anonymous didn't" drift.
-7. **Phase 42 device gate covers all 3 paths** — Julien tests Anonymous (logout, talk to coach) + BYOK (his own Anthropic key) + ServerKey (default). All 3 must work BEFORE Phase 43 starts.
-
-**Warning signs:**
-- PR diff in Phase 42 deletes tests in `test/services/coach/`. Reviewer auto-comment.
-- New `try-catch` in `coach_orchestrator.dart` — manual review checks the catch body has at least `Sentry.captureException` + rethrow OR explicit user-visible error.
-- `.listen(` without subscription tracking (Pitfall 1 cross-reference).
-- Disclaimer footer disappears in Anonymous mode (manual device gate test).
-- Backend logs `save_fact` succeeded but Flutter `CoachProfile` still missing the field (audit P0-4 entrenched).
-
-**Phase to address:**
-**Phase 42** is THE risk window. The orchestrator refactor MUST be the first commit of Phase 42 (not the last) so that the rest of the phase builds on a stable foundation, with full device-gate before scenes go on top.
-
-**Lint/test to add:**
-- Test `test/services/coach/orchestrator_invariants_test.dart` — golden test of 3-paths × 5 scenarios × disclaimer presence × breadcrumb count.
-- Test `test/services/coach/orchestrator_stream_breadcrumb_test.dart` — Stream path emits same breadcrumb names as Future path.
-- Manual: device gate before merging Phase 42 — Julien runs Anonymous + BYOK + ServerKey on iPhone.
-- Test count regression check — CI fails if `test/services/coach/` test count decreases vs `dev` branch.
