-## Executive Summary
-
-v2.9 is an additive milestone that installs a 3-level visual projection layer (vignettes inline / scenes interactives / canvas modal) directly into the existing MINT chat, delivering the verticale "onboarding-to-first-insight" in under 20 minutes. The doctrine is explicit: the coach IS the product. Every output of research converges on a single architectural posture — composition of existing infrastructure, not new procurement. Zero new dependencies are required. The entire milestone runs on `dart:async`, `fl_chart 0.70.0`, `MintPremiumSlider`, `sse-starlette 2.x`, and Pydantic v2 `to_camel`, all already validated in production.
+v2.8 n'est pas un milestone de features, c'est une intervention chirurgicale. MINT a perdu contact avec la réalité : **388 bare catches silencieux**, oracle absent, agents qui hallucinent, produit qu'on ne peut pas vérifier mécaniquement en <60s. Verdict panel unanime : les outils nécessaires **existent déjà en germe** (Sentry wirée, 12 gates CI, 8 flags, 52 redirect callbacks GoRouter, `tools/e2e_flow_smoke.sh`, SLOMonitor). **v2.8 = activer + assembler + fermer la boucle, pas construire from scratch.**
 
-The recommended build order is strictly sequential by risk and dependency: Phase 40 (pure-function backend with golden fixtures and Dart parity) is the linchpin that everything else depends on. Phase 41 (hero number and Level-1 vignettes inline) is low-risk UI that validates the visual contract before streaming is touched. Phase 42 (interactive scenes and Stream refactor) is the highest-risk phase — it touches `CoachOrchestrator`'s hot path across 3 authentication modes, and must be feature-flagged, adapter-based, and device-gated before Phase 43 starts. Phase 43 (canvas modal and Explorer deep-link) is the deepest visual layer and the safest to defer if Phase 42 burns schedule.
-
-Three structural risks dominate all four research files in near-perfect consensus: (1) the `Stream<ChatMessage>` refactor in Phase 42 is a 5-7 day P50 effort disguised as a 2-3 day task that will cascade if attempted as a big-bang rewrite; (2) the facade-sans-cablage pattern (v2.5 audit, Wave E-PRIME 42K LOC deleted) is the recurrence risk for every phase — widgets must be wired before they are written; (3) backend-to-Dart `compute_marge_fiscale` parity must be enforced by shared JSON golden fixtures from Phase 40 day one, or the live slider in Phase 42 will diverge from the server truth. Every phase must pass a physical device gate (Julien, iPhone, `flutter run --release`) before the next phase begins.
+**La boucle inverse (ce qu'on ne fait PAS)** : 0 feature produit, 0 nouveau vendor (Datadog/LaunchDarkly/Amplitude refusés), 0 migration Dio, 0 OTel, 0 Patrol/Maestro, 0 Firebase Remote Config.
 
